    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0251",
      "sequence": 263,
      "meaning": "Ten thousand kings try to lift the bow at once, yet it does not shift at all. Śiva’s bow will no more budge than a faithful woman’s mind at a libertine’s words. Every king becomes an object of ridicule, like an ascetic without detachment, and departs forcibly robbed by the bow of fame, victory and vaunted heroism. Defeated and stripped of splendour, they return to their separate places. Seeing them, Janaka grows distraught and speaks words steeped in anger: rulers from many lands came after hearing the vow; gods and demons in human bodies and countless battle-firm heroes assembled, yet none has won the lovely princess and great renown. It seems Brahmā created no victor capable of mastering the bow.",
