    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0254",
      "sequence": 266,
      "meaning": "As Lakṣmaṇa speaks in anger, the earth reels and the elephants of the quarters sway. Every world and ruler is frightened; Sītā rejoices inwardly while Janaka feels embarrassed. The guru, Raghupati and all the sages delight in their hearts and thrill again and again. With a gesture Rāma restrains Lakṣmaṇa and seats him affectionately nearby. Recognizing the auspicious moment, Viśvāmitra speaks with great tenderness: rise, Rāma; break Śiva’s bow and relieve Janaka’s anguish, dear child. Hearing the guru, Rāma bows his head at his feet; neither elation nor dismay enters his heart. He rises with natural ease, his bearing shaming a young lion. Upon the arena’s eastern-mountain platform the young sun of Raghu rises; every lotus-like saint opens, and their bee-like eyes rejoice.",
